/* ---------- Settings ---------- */
const APP_VER=325;
const WHATS_NEW=['Back buttons now return to the page you came from, even between two Settings pages (like Planning › Holidays). Planning & availability is grouped into Your week and Studio.','Notifications is tidier: the switch for this phone comes first, then quiet hours, then one “What to send” list with the evening nudge, morning digest, review reminder and work hours. Times open the same wheel everywhere.','The review reminder tells you when notifications are off on this phone, with a link to turn them on.','Settings › Reviews: pick what your weekly review covers (week in numbers, habits, goal check-ins, Inbox tidy-up), and get a reminder on your review day at a time you choose.','Settings rows that open a sheet, like Shortcut links and Working hours, now show an arrow.','Settings › Tasks, habits & capture: choose how tasks sort, your usual focus session length, and whether captures confirm with a toast. Shortcut links fold into one row.','Starter set tiles show each module’s icon, softer cards and a check when picked. Anything already on Today shows as added.','Settings › Today now holds everything that shows on Today: your cards (with icons), Top 3 and Plan tomorrow, the cards that come and go, and carry-over. Add to Today has a search and a short line for every module. Reviews is just reviews now.','A tidier Settings: four short groups (Your day, Make it yours, Connected, Your data) and a different icon for every page. Calendars now holds every calendar link, Notifications holds only notifications, Today & reviews is now Reviews & check-ins, and focus timer and habit note options moved to Tasks, habits & capture.','Clear the demo now removes all of it: tasks made from demo project steps, ideas you turned into tasks or entries, linked items, trashed copies, the automatic net-worth snapshot, and badges and bests earned on demo history (rebuilt from your own data). It also shows up in Settings › Data & help whenever demo leftovers are still around.','Rewards: a ring beside the date fills as today gets done, and a new Done page collects everything you finished. Tap the ring to see the split.','Habit cards show your streak, and you earn a streak freeze every 7 days or 4 weeks in a row. Miss a day and Life OS offers one the next morning.','Life areas level up as you make progress, projects fill as their tasks get done, and Reviews now holds badges and your personal bests. Some badges unlock new palettes.','Turn ideas into plans and they grow in your Inbox garden. Your weekly review opens with your score, Studio shows a lock once a week is committed, and the evening Plan tomorrow card says what kind of day is coming. Everything is in Settings › Rewards.','Every life area page now follows the same layout: your note, one line, what’s special to the area, your goals and projects, then its modules.','Your weekly review now opens with your week in numbers: a line for each module you used, compared with last week, and one thing worth noticing.','New: a starter set. Pick what you want to keep track of and Life OS turns on those modules and puts the daily ones on Today. In Settings › Today it only adds, never moves what you have.','Today can change with the time of day: a different order for mornings, the day and evenings. Turn it on in Settings › Today. It never reshuffles while you’re looking.','Log in plain words from Quick capture: “meditated 20 min”, “spent 42 at Wegmans”. Any log module works, including your own (add its words when you edit it). Return logs it, with Undo.','Every module card on Today now does something: log again, tick off what’s due, see days to the next date, or what needs you.','New: Settings › Today. Reorder, hide and show the sections on Today, and add any module as a card you can use right there, like logging your energy in one tap. Each card can be full or one line, and show always, mornings, evenings or until it’s done.','“Today” no longer squashes in date tiles, and every log shares one year card. Relationships shows the next date and thank-yous owed, says “Today” instead of a red 0, and folds past events in grey.','Movies hides empty tabs, Restaurants, Points and Insurance put the status or amount on the right with only close dates in red, Compass’s Edit moved to the … menu, and Life admin gets a summary line.','Learning: books you’re reading are compact rows with +10 on the row, courses are one row each with the next lesson and a tick, and the Learning page counts lessons instead of percent.','Courses says “0 of 3 hours this week”, new flashcards aren’t red, empty paths say “No steps yet”, and School planner says “Due” once.','Home: the next three things coming up, your car as one row, and module rows that say something (“Oil change overdue”, “Moving day not set”).','Far-off chores show a date, empty headings are gone, warranties are only colored when they end soon, places like Freezer and Kitchen are singular again, and Inventory and Improvements put the money on the right. Moving asks for your moving day.','Health: your main modules are always listed, the next three appointments show, and your note is back under the title. Every module page now puts + before ….','Workouts has an add field, Quick log wraps, the dinner planner is lighter, Meal prep and Care are tidier, the energy calendar waits for data, the check-in reminder moved to the … menu, and Sleep, Cycle and Symptoms read in plain words.','Finances: the next three bills on the page, module rows that say something (“$1,867 next 30 days”), and an add field on Spending: type “Wegmans 42” and press Enter.','Net worth now counts your Investments accounts and hides the chart until there are two months. Savings goals are compact rows, bills drop “Pay by hand”, returns put the return-by date first, IOUs and wishlists read more clearly, and Investments shows balances on the right.','Family: a summary under the title, module rows that show the next event and each child’s balance, and chips to see one person at a time.','School & activities says when nothing’s coming up and folds past events without crossing them out. Sizes & info shows the kind on the right. Allowance shows one balance per child, a one-tap “Pay” button, and + or − on every amount.','Community: a summary under the title (“14 h volunteered and $70 given this year”), real numbers on the module rows, and your note back on the page.','Logs like Volunteering, Giving and Faith practice show the number on the right and the date under the name, share one year card, drop the year from this year’s month headings, and offer “Log it again” on long-press. Giving mentions receipts only when one is missing.','Life area pages: your note sits under the title, goals and projects show as rings with open tasks folded into one line, and the modules are one compact list. Every module page now opens with the same add field as Organize.','Career: the next two 1:1s, one “Was this a win?” at a time, small level dots for skills, stage chips and a … menu in Job search, a fixed Side business line, and clearer follow-up dates.','Organize feels like one app: every page opens with the same add field, list rows lose their arrows, and Inbox drops the repeated “→ Task” and shows an age like “6 wk” on older ideas instead of a sub-heading.','Tasks keeps nudges like “Review 2 cards” under “Also today”. A habit’s milestones are one line, Routines drops the Up next card, a routine’s end time and runs share a line, and a project keeps up to 5 done tasks in its list.','Routines: each row says when it runs, today’s come first, and a tick replaces play once it’s done. On a routine, a round tick beside Run marks it done, steps drag to reorder, runs are one line, and Repeats and Time sit in Details.','Projects look like Goals now: a ring, then the next task with a small tick, soonest first, with dates like “6 weeks left”. Lists get icons and lose their bars, and Edit and Add a section moved into the … menu.','Goals: each goal is two lines, with its next milestone and a small tick in the grey line. Thinner rings in one colour, area headings that just count goals, the soonest goal first, and dates like “By Dec 2027” when they’re far off. The chips match the other pages and Done hides when empty.','On a goal’s page, ticked milestones stay in the list, a + by the heading adds one, Check in is a quiet link until one is due, an empty “Moves it forward” is a single link, and Edit lives in the … menu.','Habits hides the chip row when “All” would be the only chip, and “Show more” lines in lists use a normal divider.','Habits: two lines each, with this week’s dots on the right, thinner rings, and no +1 button (tap the ring). Habits due today come first, then each area, and ones you’ve finished fold into “done today”. Streaks show from 3 with a small flame.','The chips are just All, Today and Paused, and area headings read “3 habits” until the week gets going. A habit’s page has this week as seven tappable days, and History switches between Month and Year.','Tasks: Replan sits before the fold arrow in Overdue, and the add box matches the other pages. Sticky bars only draw a line once you scroll.','Swipe a task left to move it straight to tomorrow, with Undo. Hold it for other days.','Tasks: Replan sits in the Overdue heading and its sheet counts chores too, chores show their area icon (swipe right still finishes them), and Overdue shows 5 at a time.','Next 7 days has a small + on each day instead of an “Add to…” row, and life-area items sit on their day. Area names are icons on each row, tasks with steps keep a plain circle, and there’s a folded No date section with “done today” quietly at the end.','The filter sheet shows how many tasks each choice has, quick add’s chips stand out, holding a long task shows its full title, and the Replan button reads “Replan 4 tasks”.','Every row in Tasks now has its divider line, lined up with the rest.','A calmer Inbox: no buttons on each row. Tap the green “→ place” to move an idea there, swipe right to do the same, or hold for more. Plain icons, no ages on newer ideas, and Tidy up sits beside the title.','Pinned ideas have their own group at the top, the edit sheet asks “Where should it go?” with the same places as everywhere else, moving says “Added to Courses” with Undo, and Tidy up starts with ideas that already have a place.','Life area pickers show each area’s icon. Quick days no longer offer Monday twice when Monday is tomorrow, and on a weekend the chip reads Next weekend.','Picking where an idea goes uses the same grouped picker everywhere, with search and the current place marked. Tidy up names the place it will save to.','Plan and Snooze open a short sheet of quick days (Tomorrow, This weekend, Next week…) with a date field for anything else, and a snoozed idea tells you the date it comes back.','The … menu on ideas is shorter, the Move button is a small arrow so titles have room, and the file sheet counts only what’s ticked.','Every Inbox group has File all, including Other places and Not sure yet. In the file sheet, tap where an idea is going to change it.','Each idea’s Move button has a … next to it: move it somewhere else, or change what Inbox suggests for it. The To buy / To read chips are gone.','Inbox is one card grouped by where each idea goes, with File all per group and a “Not sure yet” group last. Older ideas sit under an “Over a month old” line, Tidy up folds into one line, the add box stays at the top as you scroll, and reviews live in More.','Even dividers in Tasks, and days still to come are plain faint dots on Habits.','A tidier Inbox: one add box like the other pages, quick tags only while you type, one Tidy up card instead of three banners, sort in the … menu, and icon-only “→” chips for long names.','Tasks: section headings sit inside their cards, the overdue chip and section agree, Filter, Group and Search are icons, life-area items say what they are, and check-ins ask a question with a Later button.','Habits: area headings say how many you’ve met, bigger week dots with today ringed (tap one to log that day), and counts on every filter chip. The weekly review only lists habits that need you.','Goals: no repeated “Next”, and the Timeline view is gone. Every hold menu reads Open first and Delete last, more quick actions have Undo, and Details rows look the same on habits and goals.','Goals list: one card with area headings, progress rings with each area’s icon, “3 of 5 milestones · 21 weeks left”, the next milestone to tick, a Check in chip when one is due, sort by area, date or progress, and a Timeline view. Type “Run a half marathon by April” to add one.','Each goal’s page shows why it matters, a solid Check in button when due, the next milestone highlighted, dates on milestones, drag to reorder, “Add as a task” from a milestone’s hold menu, a place to link habits and projects, fuller Details, check-in history as coloured dots, and a chart for number goals.','Check-ins show your last one, mood colours and one step for the week that becomes a task. New goals get quick dates, suggested milestones and a “Supported by” habit. The weekly review asks about goals that are due.','Habits list: the same icon rings as Today (tap to log), this week as seven dots, one card with life-area headings, +1 on count habits, area chips instead of a menu, and a quick add box that reads “Stretch every morning”. Missed-yesterday habits rise to the top.','Each habit’s page has its streak, best, this month and total up top, a solid Done button, a big − / + counter for count habits, milestones, the last 12 months as squares, and Details for time of day, reminder, After another habit, and Pause or end.','Skip any habit from its hold menu without breaking the streak, and the weekly review lists each habit’s week with an offer to ease a target that keeps slipping.','Tasks is calmer: follow-ups and wishlist prompts sit in Check-ins instead of Overdue, life-area items due this week get their own group, and the next 7 days is one list with “Add to Tuesday” rows. Sections show counts and fold.','Rows say “3 weeks late”, “1 of 3 steps” and how a task repeats. Swipe left for Tomorrow, This weekend, Next week or a day. Hold for project and life area too.','The overdue chip opens Replan (now with Move all to today and Drop), tasks a month late ask if you’re still doing them, and the header has Group by, Search and saved views.','The task sheet puts When right under the title, with life area, project and priority as chips and a How long setting. Done shows each day with its count.','Inbox, round two: type an idea straight into the box, with starters for To buy, To read, To watch and Gift ideas. Each idea shows an icon, its first note line, and a green dot when it’s new; month-old ages turn amber.','Filter Inbox by where ideas go, file them all in one sheet, merge look-alikes, snooze, pin, give an idea a life area, and act on several at once. Gift ideas fill in who they’re for. Saved links get their real page titles.','Tidy up: swipe right for a task, left to delete, up for later; the main button files to the right place, and the end shows what you did. It’s also in the weekly review and on Today when ideas pile up. More shows the Inbox count.','Inbox is tidier: tighter rows with dividers, titles on two lines with their age underneath, links shown by page and site.','Each idea can suggest its home (→ Gifts, → Reading, → Task) and files there in one tap. Press and hold for Do it today, Plan for a day or Move.','A Tidy up button goes through ideas one at a time, and a nudge offers to review or clear ideas older than a month. Reviews waiting get their own row.','The capture box has a mic, and the capture sheet says when Return will save.','On More, pinned and life area circles line up in the same columns, with less space between the two rows.','Month has a Calendar view: switch from Overview to see each day’s all-day items and events by name, the way a wall calendar does. Tap a day for its details below.','Month and quarter now share one calm day cell: the date with a small load dot, a ring for holidays. Holidays are listed under each month with their icon, and the day panel shows events with a colour bar and to-dos with a tick.','Calendar’s week view tells things apart at a glance: all-day items are soft pills (holidays with their icon), timed events have a colour bar, and to-dos with a time have a small circle. Times line up in one column.','Plan a session shades the days you’ve already planned on its calendar. Tap a shaded day to take it off; Remove no longer asks to undo.','A habit’s By month section is now a short list: full month names, a meter against your target and the percent. Tap a month to see it in History.','The chip row under the week strip stays at one height and only scrolls sideways.','Habit rings on Today are bigger, with bigger icons, and a lighter, thinner ring to match priorities.','Clearer habit icons: a lotus for meditating, a glass for water, a phone with a line through it for screen-free time, a speech bubble for languages, a stretching figure, a notebook for journaling and an open book for reading.','Priority rings on Today are lighter and thinner, so the list reads calmer.','Holidays on Today now carry their own icon, with just the holiday’s name. Tap one to open Holidays & days off.','Each holiday has its own icon: a turkey for Thanksgiving, a tree for Christmas, a party popper for New Year’s, fireworks for the Fourth.','US holidays are on by default, with a new Settings page: Holidays & days off. Pick which ones you take off, add the day after Thanksgiving or Christmas Eve, and use observed dates for weekend holidays.','On a day off your work hours clear: Today reads “Thanksgiving · day off”, free time counts the whole day and Plan my day leaves it alone.','Studio plans holidays to half capacity, never suggests work tasks for them, and gives you a heads-up the week before. Your weekly review does too.','Holidays have their own quiet ring in the week strip, the date picker and Calendar, and the quarter view lists each month’s holidays.','The week, month and quarter picker is tidier: even padding, centred dates, pill months and the current period softly marked.','Tap the title in Studio or Calendar to jump to any week, month or quarter, the same way you pick a day on Today.','With iPhone’s Increase Contrast on, chips keep their light fill; habit counts line up under the name; “Show more” reads as a link.','Fixes from the module review: chips without stray rings, even dividers, sentence case everywhere, a date picker that opens on this month, a tidier Quick capture, honest Studio counts, “All” links, “Goal met”-style habit groups, quieter Settings and a cleaner demo.','Behind the scenes: every colour, size, icon, line, shadow, timing and breakpoint now comes from one set of design tokens, so the app looks consistent everywhere and palettes reach every corner.','Calmer components: one card shape, soft buttons in two heights, grey header links, one chip and field style, quieter segmented controls and priority rings, a softer + button, a pill on the active tab, light toasts and menus, aligned rows and dividers, and finished items faded and struck through.','A calmer foundation: lighter weights, an even spacing and type scale, thinner bars, lighter checkboxes, cards on a hairline, softer sheets and a calmer spring. Palettes now recolour everything.','Polish round 5: pinned shortcuts as circles, calmer habit rings and Studio rows, “Goal met” when you pass a weekly target, quiet empty modules, simpler charts and matching money figures.','Bigger, easier-to-see icons in lists, settings, pinned tiles and life area modules.','Life areas on More are back on one line you can swipe through, with larger icons in each circle.','Calmer and lighter everywhere: softer card shadows, page buttons and selected filters in soft green, plain icons in rows, lighter switches and charts, and page titles a size smaller.','Calendar: lighter heat in Quarter, one quiet dot per day in Month, plain dates in Week, no plane icon over trip rings, and the trip name no longer repeats under the next month.','A lighter feel: text a size smaller, lighter weights for titles, labels, links and buttons, and softer priority rings.','Polish round 4: pages slide in (no blank flash); Habits page flat like Goals; filled icon for the active tab; one progress bar thickness; neutral section headings; life-area tiles lead with the number; calm trend colours; quieter sheet fields; one size for secondary text; one Add-a-task line and one footer line on Today; past calendar days fade; quiet add rows; one card padding.','Fixes: a second dot under some week-strip days, the Habits grid on Today sitting outside the card, and a stray “·” before time left in Schedule.','Polish round 3: one solid button per screen; a frosted bottom bar; search and sort moved into the ••• menu; lighter tick circles; dates as plain text; overdue tasks as a soft “carried over” row; quiet “Add a note” lines in life areas; month names open their month; a gentler swipe hint; dividers start at the text; one size for big numbers; tasks show their life area; softer chevrons.','Polish round 2: week-strip dots only for deadlines and all-day items; habits show one progress line; sage calendar heat; Inbox ages in words; one Filter button on Tasks; flatter Goals and Projects; quieter empty states in cards; Pinned tiles and life-area chips on More; Studio bars show what’s planned; one line for past reviews; finished priorities step back; “No tasks yet” instead of 0 of 0; light toasts; smaller sheet titles; list progress bars; quieter section links.','Polish: one row of chips under Today’s week strip; red only for things that are late; Inbox chores on one quiet line; roomier Studio habit row; back links name the page you came from; sentence-case section labels; the small title bar arrives sooner; life area modules as a grid; one toast at a time.','Scroll down any page and the small title bar now has a back button.','Date picker: only this month’s days show, with no extra row from the next month.','Studio: Spread them no longer piles extra sessions onto days a habit already has, and the card hides once there’s no free day left this week.','The habit note bar closes when you leave the page.','Demo: real amounts for bills, pay and purchases, a believable odometer, and plainer notes.','Fuller demo: Settings › Data & help › Try the demo now also fills next quarter and next year, older history, finished and paused goals and projects, and week, month and quarter focuses.','Toasts sit above a sheet’s Add button instead of covering it. Settings › Display & motion › Stronger borders brings card edges back again. The Top 3 pick sheet’s field and + button are round.','New task: no stray line above Add a step when there are no steps yet.','Date picker: quick picks fit and use soft fills, tighter day rows, and no hard outlines with Increase Contrast on.','More compact: less padding inside cards and between sections everywhere, so more fits on screen.','A softer look: cards lift off the page instead of sitting in outlines, buttons and switches are rounder, text and controls are a size bigger, and sections sit closer together. Nothing moved and everything works the same. With iPhone’s Increase Contrast on, cards keep a faint edge instead of a dark outline.','Import tasks: More › Import tasks brings in a Todoist or TickTick CSV, any CSV with a title column, or a pasted list. You see everything first, and Undo takes it all back.','Evening habit nudge: one notification at 8 PM (or your time) with the habits still open that day. Nothing is sent if they’re all done. Settings › Today & reviews.','Skip holidays: with holidays on, a repeating task or block can skip them. The holiday says what was skipped.','Unscheduled tray: under the week timeline, drag a to-do onto a day and hour to give it a time.','Priority grid: Tasks › views › Priority grid sorts open tasks into Do now, Plan, Quick and Later. Drag a task (or use the arrow keys) to move it.','Invite files: in Quick capture, tap Invite file and pick an .ics. It opens as a time block with its title, time, place and notes.','Under the hood: status pills, menus, stat rows, row ends and empty states each come from one shared piece, and Today and Calendar share one time grid.'];
/* an unread What's new counts as one thing in the Inbox (its badge) until it's opened or dismissed */
function newVerN(){const s=get.settings();return typeof s.seenVer==='number'&&s.seenVer<APP_VER?1:0;}
function whatsNewCard(){if(!newVerN())return null;return el('div',{class:'focus-chip wncard'},IconTile(null,{html:ic('star',IC.sm),style:'border-radius:var(--r-row)'}),el('button',{class:'grow small',style:'text-align:left;min-height:var(--size-32)',onclick:()=>{whatsNew();App.refresh();}},`What’s new in Life OS ${APP_VER}`),el('button',{class:'fa',onclick:()=>{whatsNew();App.refresh();}},'See ›'),IconButton('Dismiss',{size:'sm',html:ic('x',IC.xs),onclick:()=>setSettings({seenVer:APP_VER})}));}
function whatsNew(){setSettings({seenVer:APP_VER});const inst=openSheet({title:`What’s new in ${APP_VER}`,left:{label:'Close'},build:b=>b.append(el('div',{class:'list'},WHATS_NEW.map(t=>Row({as:'div',style:'align-items:flex-start;padding-block:var(--s3)'},el('span',{style:'display:grid;color:var(--action-text);margin-top:var(--nudge)',html:ic('check',IC.sm)}),el('span',{class:'grow'},t)))))});return inst;}
